  {
   "url": "https://www.fs.usda.gov/r09/shawnee/maps-guides",
   "status": 200,
   "final_url": "https://www.fs.usda.gov/r09/shawnee/maps-guides",
   "title": "Shawnee National Forest | Visitor Maps and Guides | Forest Service",
   "text": "Skip to main content\nAn official website of the United States government\nHere's how you know\nForest Service\nU.S. DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE\nShawnee National Forest\nHome\nVisit\nTopics\nResources\nAbout\nSearch\nForest Service Home Inside the Forest Service About the Agency\nAlerts and Fire Danger Status\nBreadcrumb\nForest Service Home Eastern Region Shawnee National Forest Visitor Maps and Guides\nT\nT\nT\nAlerts\nEvents\nPasses\nPermits\nRecreation\nSafety and Outdoor Ethics\nVisitor Maps and Guides\nVisitor Maps and Guides\nIMPORTANT: Beginning April 2026, the Forest Service can no longer update or add new digital maps to the Avenza Map Store. When a paper map is updated, the previous digital version will be removed from the store and not replaced. Digital maps that have not yet been updated will remain available on the store. MVUMs are reissued each year. It is the responsibility of motor vehicle users to acquire the current MVUM.\nA variety of maps for the Shawnee National Forest are available at our offices or online. For map descriptions and details on how to obtain maps see below.\nForest Guide Map\nLooking to get oriented to the forest? The forest guide map provides a general map of the Forest, roads and land ownership, as well as locations of our main recreation sites.\nDownload Forest Guide Map\nVisitor Brochures & Trail Maps\nBrochures with Site Maps\nDigital Trail Maps\nMotor Vehicle Use Maps\nThis map shows Forest Service roads (e.g., roads administered by Shawnee National Forest), road numbers, and road closure dates. Currently the paper map is out of print, so this map is only available online.\nAll Maps\nHidden Springs District MVUM\nMississippi Bluffs District MVUM\nPaper Maps\nA large fold out Shawnee National Forest map is available for purchase ($14) at our offices or online through the United States Geological Service Store.\nDetailed trail maps are available through the Friends of the Shawnee, just follow the link below for more information and online ordering.\nPurchase Online through Friends of the Shawnee Store\nAdditional Maps and Information\nRiver to River Trail Maps\nThe 160-mile River to River Trail spans southern Illinois from the Ohio River to the Mississippi River. Download free geo-referenced maps.\nGeospatial Data\nRoads and motorized trails, forest boundary data, and Forest Service ownership data for Shawnee National Forest.\nSurvey Records\nForest Regulations\nAs a visitor to the National Forest, you are asked to follow certain rules designed to protect the Forest, natural resources and to provide for public safety of visitors.\nShawnee Wilderness and Watershed Closure Order\nOutlines restrictions in wilderness and watershed areas, including stock use with accompanying map.\nLast updated July 24, 2026\nReturn to top\nShawnee National Forest Supervisor’s Office\n50 Hwy 145 South\nHarrisburg, IL 62946\n618-253-7114\nDistrict Offices\nFollow Us on Social Media\nX\nFacebook\nFlickr\nPrimary Footer Menu\nRecreation.gov\nAccessibility Statement\nVisit OIG\nOur Performance\nAnti-Harassment Policy\nCareers\nUSA.gov\nWhiteHouse.gov\nPrivacy Policy\nPlain Writing\nNo Fear Act Data\nFOIA\nReport Fraud on USDA Contracts\nPolicies and Links\neGov\nNon-Discrimination Statement\nOpen Government\nInformation Quality\nForest Service\nU.S. DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE\nX\nFacebook\nYoutube\nFlickr\nInstagram",
