   "title": "Ray Norbut State Fish and Wildlife Area",
   "text": "Skip to main content\nILLINOISDEPARTMENTOF NATURALRESOURCES\nJ.B. Pritzker,\nGovernorillinois.gov\nSEARCH\nAnnouncements\nNOW AVAILABLE: Request a Mail-in CWD Testing Kit Today!\nMORE INFO\nPLAN\nPUBLIC HUNTING\nSPECIES\nDATA\nRESOURCES\nRay Norbut State Fish and Wildlife Area\nPage Contents\nSite Contact Info\nSite Maps\nSite Characteristics\nSite Specific Regulations\nDeer\nTurkey\nWaterfowl\nUpland & Small Game\nFurbearers\nAmenities\nSite Contact Info\nOffice phone: (217) 392-2345\nOffice address: P.O. 203 Augusta, IL 62311. Main Office is at Weinberg-King State Park.\nSite coordinates: 39.68485, -90.64865\nCounty: Pike\nSite Superintendent\nDistrict Wildlife Biologist\nConservation Police\nSite Closures List\nSite Maps\nDigital Map\nPrintable Map\nSite Characteristics\nHuntable acres: 1,290\nHabitat: This area is rolling with steep hills and deep hollows, covered with mature timber of oak-hickory type. The entire area is well supplied with water from springs interspersed throughout the area. Agricultural leases maintain open areas to provide habitat diversity.\nActive habitat management will be occurring throughout the year on the site, including prescribed burning.\nSite Specific Regulations\nStatewide and associated species regulations apply at the site unless noted hereafter.\nSite requires use of windshield card, displayed on vehicle dashboard, to report hunting effort and harvest by 15 February.\nHunters may leave stands unattended. Stands must be portable and labeled with owner’s name, address and telephone number.\nDeer\nArchery\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nFirearm\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except that a site-specific permit, issued through the statewide lottery, is required.\nLate Winter Antlerless\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except that the season will be open by public announcement each fall.\nMuzzleloader\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except that a Pike County Muzzleloader Permit, issued through the statewide lottery, is required. Note: Muzzeloader permits are not valid at site during the second portion of the regular firearm deer season.\nSpecial CWD\nNot available at this site.\nYouth Firearm\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nTurkey\nFall Archery\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nFall Shotgun\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nSpring\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nYouth Spring\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nWaterfowl\nDucks, Coots, & Mergansers\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nGoose\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nSnipe & Rail\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nYouth Waterfowl\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nUpland & Small Game\nDove\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except:\nHunters must hunt at staked sites from September 1-5.\nA non-toxic shot is required.\nRabbit\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nSquirrel\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nUpland Birds\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nWoodcock\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply.\nFurbearers\nHunting\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except:\nCoyote and skunk seasons run concurrently with the statewide fox season.\nGroundhog hunting not permitted.\nNo centerfire rifles permitted.\nTrapping\nAvailable at this site. Statewide regulations apply, except that a special permit is required. Drawing is held on odd number years and publicly announced.\nAmenities\nMore Information\nPRINT HUNTING SITE INFO\nPrivacy\n|\nContact Us\n|\nWebsite by:",
