  {
   "url": "https://www.mass.gov/locations/farnham-connolly-state-park",
   "status": 200,
   "final_url": "https://www.mass.gov/locations/farnham-connolly-state-park",
   "title": "Farnham-Connolly State Park | Mass.gov",
   "text": "An official website of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts\nHere's how you know\nSkip to main content\nMenu\nLanguage\nState Organizations\nMass.gov\nSearch terms\nSEARCH\nParks & Recreation Visit Massachusetts State Parks\nFarnham-Connolly State Park\nTHIS PAGE, FARNHAM-CONNOLLY STATE PARK, IS\nOFFERED BY\nDepartment of Conservation & Recreation\nFarnham-Connolly State Park\nAddress\n705 Neponset St., Canton, MA 02021\nDirections\nPhone\nCaptain House - Blue Hills (617) 698-1802\nWHEELCHAIR ACCESSIBLE\nDOGS ALLOWED\nHISTORIC SITE\nGet Directions\nto Farnham-Connolly State Park in Google Maps\nDETAILS\nOverview\nHours\nParking\nAll Activities\nFacilities\nAccessibility\nRestrictions\nMore info\nRelated parks\nOverview\nPaved trails, numerous plants and wetland wildlife provide opportunities to connect with nature. Located at the former Canton Airport, this six-acre park is ideal for passive recreation.\nHours\nDawn to dusk\nParking\nSmall parking area.\nAll Activities\nNature trails\nBird watching\nHiking\nFacilities\nScenic overlooks\nShade pavilion\nLoop trail\nInterpretive signage\nNative plantings\nYear-round accessible portable toilet on site\nAccessibility\nPaved paths\nRestrictions\nNo alcohol\nNo off-road vehicles\nMore info\nThe park falls within the Fowl Meadow and Ponkapoag Bog ACEC. The Fowl Meadow area includes the largest wetland and floodplain areas in the Neponset River basin.\nRelated parks\nBlue Hills Reservation\nMore parks\nVisit Massachusetts State Parks Locations\nHiking in Massachusetts State Parks Locations\nHelp Us Improve Mass.gov\nwith your feedback\nDid you find what you were looking for on this webpage?\nYes\nNo\nMass.gov\nState Organizations\nDigital Accessibility Statement\nPrivacy Policy\nSite Policies\nPublic Records Requests\n© 2026 Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\nMass.gov® is a registered service mark of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\nFeedback",
